{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/688", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"write a play where tamil and sanskrit argue themselves on superiority\\n\", \"response\": \"Here's a short play where Tamil and Sanskrit argue about their superiority:\\n\\nTitle: The Language Debate\\n\\n(The stage is set with two chairs, one for Tamil and one for Sanskrit. The lights come up, and Tamil and Sanskrit enter the stage and take their seats.)\\n\\nTamil: Good evening, Sanskrit. I'm glad we're finally able to have this conversation about the superiority of our languages.\\n\\nSanskrit: Indeed, Tamil. I'm eager to discuss this matter. I believe that Sanskrit is the most superior language in the world.\\n\\nTamil: Oh, really? I think Tamil is the best language out there. It's rich in history and has a unique grammar and syntax.\\n\\nSanskrit: But Sanskrit is the language of the Vedas and the Upanishads, the ancient texts of India. It's the language of spirituality and philosophy.\\n\\nTamil: True, but Tamil has its own set of ancient texts, such as the Tirukkural, which are considered some of the greatest works of literature in the world.\\n\\nSanskrit: However, Sanskrit is a more logical and analytical language, while Tamil is more emotional and expressive.\\n\\nTamil: That's not true! Tamil has a rich literary tradition that has produced some of the greatest poets and writers in history.\\n\\nSanskrit: But Sanskrit is the language of the Vedas and the Upanishads, the ancient texts of India. It's the language of spirituality and philosophy.\\n\\nTamil: True, but Tamil has its own set of ancient texts, such as the Tirukkural, which are considered some of the greatest works of literature in the world.\\n\\nSanskrit: However, Sanskrit is a more logical and analytical language, while Tamil is more emotional and expressive.\\n\\nTamil: That's not true! Tamil has a rich literary tradition that has produced some of the greatest poets and writers in history.\\n\\nSanskrit: In conclusion, both languages have their own unique strengths and weaknesses. The superiority of a language cannot be determined by a single factor. It's up to each individual to decide which language they prefer and find most useful.\\n\\n(The lights dim, and Tamil and Sanskrit exit the stage.)\\n\\nNote: This is a fictional play, and the arguments made by Tamil and Sanskrit are not necessarily reflective of real-life opinions or beliefs. The purpose of the play is to entertain and provide a light-hearted look at the topic of language superiority.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/459", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I am using an Aura-based experience builder site. On the site  I have a lwc that I have enabled Light DOM for. I am doing this because I want to target a child button element from a sibling Aura component that is using an external Js library called IntroJS. IntroJs needs to target an element in order to attatch tour steps.\\n\\nAfter enabling the Light DOM, I am able to enter the chrome console and use document.Query selector and I get a result however when I use document.querySelector from the Aura component I get null. Why is that?\", \"response\": \"There could be several reasons why you are getting null when using document.querySelector from your Aura component, even though you are able to select the element using the Chrome console. Here are a few possible explanations:\\n\\n1. Scope: The Light DOM of a Lightning Web Component is not visible to the Shadow DOM of an Aura component. This means that the Aura component may not be able to access the Light DOM elements of the LWC, and therefore, the element you are trying to target may be invisible to the Aura component.\\n\\n2. Timing: It's possible that the element you are trying to target is not yet available when the Aura component is trying to access it. This could be due to the element being dynamically created or because the page has not finished loading.\\n\\n3. Syntax: It's possible that you are using the wrong syntax or selector when trying to target the element from the Aura component. Make sure that the selector you are using is correct and matches the element you are trying to target.\\n\\n4. Permissions: The Aura component may not have the necessary permissions to access the Light DOM elements of the LWC. Make sure that the LWC is marked as \\\"accessible\\\" to the Aura component in the LWC's metadata.\\n\\nTo troubleshoot this issue, you can try the following:\\n\\n- Use the Chrome console to check if the element is dynamically created or only available after a certain event.\\n- Use console.log statements to verify that the element is available and visible to the Aura component.\\n- Check the syntax and selector used in the document.querySelector call from the Aura component.\\n- Verify that the LWC is marked as \\\"accessible\\\" to the Aura component in the LWC's metadata.\\n\\nBy troubleshooting these possible issues, you should be able to identify the root cause of the problem and find a solution to target the child button element from the sibling Aura component.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/445", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Use these categories:\\n\\nfinancial calculators\\nmeasurement calculators\\nmath calculators\\ndate and time calculators\\nastrology calculators\\nhealth calculators\\nhome calculators\\nstatistics calculators\\ngaming calculators\\npersonal finance calculators\\nfun calculators\\n\\nAnd categorize the following term:\\n\\nhigh school gpa calculator\", \"response\": \"The term \\\"high school gpa calculator\\\" would fall under the category of \\\"math calculators.\\\" GPA (Grade Point Average) is a numerical representation of a student's academic performance and is calculated by dividing the total number of grade points earned by the total number of credit hours attempted. A GPA calculator is a tool that helps students and parents calculate a student's GPA based on their grades and credit hours.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/277", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I require your assistance to draft some articles.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI’m happy to help. Please let me know what the articles are about, and any specific information you want me to include.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nIn my messages that I send you later, I will refer to this information as Information About Myself. \\n \\n\\n Here is a bit of information about myself that I want you to know. I am a solicitor and construction lawyer with more than 10 years experience specialising in construction law. I regularly advise homeowners and builders regarding their contractual and legal rights. I represent homeowners and builders in NSW, Australia as well as all courts of competent jurisdiction. I have advised homeowners, builders, and contractors experience regarding latent conditions. I have advised them on their contract rights, risks and obligations. I have negotiated and amended contracts to reflect their intentions.\", \"response\": \"Sure, I'd be happy to help you draft some articles based on the information you provided about yourself. Here are a few ideas:\\n \\n\\n 1. \\\"10 Years of Experience in Construction Law: A Q&A with a Specialist Solicitor\\\"\\n \\n\\n In this article, you could provide more details about your background and experience in construction law. You could also answer common questions that homeowners and builders have about their contractual and legal rights. This would be a great opportunity to showcase your expertise and establish yourself as a thought leader in the field.\\n \\n\\n 2. \\\"Latent Conditions in Construction: What You Need to Know\\\"\\n \\n\\n In this article, you could discuss the concept of latent conditions in construction and how they can impact homeowners and builders. You could provide practical advice on how to identify and address latent conditions, and how to negotiate and amend contracts to reflect their intentions. This would be a useful resource for anyone involved in a construction project.\\n \\n\\n 3. \\\"From Concept to Completion: A Guide to Construction Law\\\"\\n \\n\\n In this article, you could provide a comprehensive overview of construction law, from the initial planning stages to the completion of a project. You could discuss the various types of contracts and agreements involved, the legal rights and obligations of homeowners and builders, and the common issues that can arise during a construction project. This would be a valuable resource for anyone looking to better understand the complexities of construction law.\\n \\n\\n I hope these ideas are helpful. Let me know if you would like me to draft some sample articles based on this information, or if you have any other questions or requests.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/493", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Analyze this outline and write me the introduction of YouTube video titled \\\"UFC Story : He Fights Like Bruce Lee - Zabit Magomedsharipov\\\" :\\n\\nInstructions:\\n\\nIntroduction: In the introduction, begin by introducing the fighter and his fighting name. Next, provide a brief overview of his fighting style and key qualities. Use a casual tone, but be sure to convey the necessary information.\\n\\nBackground: In the background section, provide more information about where the fighter grew up and how he got into the fighting sports. Use a casual tone, but be sure to include important details about the fighter's background.\\n\\nFighting history: In the fighting history section, provide an overview of the beginning of the fighter's career and his fights in other organizations before the UFC. Use a casual tone, but be sure to provide important details about the fighter's career.\\n\\nEarly fights: In the early fights section, show footage of the fighter's early fights in other organizations. Be sure to include key moments from these fights to keep the viewer engaged.\\n\\nUFC debut: In the UFC debut section, show the fighter's debut in the UFC and highlight key moments from the fight. Use a casual tone, but be sure to convey the excitement of the fight.\\n\\nTraining: In the training section, show footage of the fighter's training and preparation for his next fight. Use a casual tone, but be sure to provide insight into the fighter's training routine.\\n\\nNext opponent: In the next opponent section, introduce the fighter's next opponent and show highlights to make them look more dangerous. Use a casual tone, but be sure to provide important details about the opponent.\\n\\nStaredowns: In the staredowns section, show footage of the staredowns between the fighter and his opponent. Use a casual tone, but be sure to convey the tension between the two fighters.\\n\\nFinal fight: In the final fight section, show the final fight between the fighter and his opponent and highlight key moments. Use a casual tone, but be sure to convey the excitement of the fight.\\n\\nOutcome: In the outcome section, always show who won the fight. Use a casual tone, but be sure to provide important details about the outcome.\", \"response\": \"Hey there, in this video we're going to talk about the UFC fighter Zabit Magomedsharipov. He's a Russian mixed martial artist who's known for his incredible fighting skills and his unique fighting style. He's been compared to the legendary Bruce Lee, and he's definitely one of the most exciting fighters in the UFC today.\\n\\nZabit grew up in Russia, and he started training in martial arts at a young age. He quickly developed a passion for fighting, and he began competing in various combat sports. He had a successful career in kickboxing and Muay Thai, and he eventually made the transition to mixed martial arts.\\n\\nZabit's fighting style is a mix of different martial arts disciplines, including Muay Thai, kickboxing, and Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu. He's known for his incredible striking skills, and he's able to mix up his attacks with both punches and kicks. He's also a skilled grappler, and he's able to use his wrestling and Jiu-Jitsu skills to take down his opponents and secure submissions.\\n\\nZabit made his UFC debut in 2017, and he quickly made a name for himself as one of the most exciting fighters in the organization. He's known for his incredible speed and agility, and he's able to move around the octagon with ease. He's also known for his incredible striking skills, and he's able to land powerful punches and kicks with ease.\\n\\nIn this video, we're going to take a closer look at Zabit's fighting style and his career in the UFC. We'll also take a look at some of his most impressive fights, and we'll discuss his potential as a future champion in the UFC. So sit back, relax, and let's take a closer look at Zabit Magomedsharipov, the fighter who fights like Bruce Lee.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/8", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Please give us creative product ideas related to air fresheners.\", \"response\": \"Sure, here are some creative product ideas related to air fresheners:\\n\\n1. Aromatherapy air fresheners: These air fresheners use essential oils to create a soothing and relaxing atmosphere. They can be used in the home, office, or car and can help to reduce stress and anxiety.\\n\\n2. Natural air fresheners: These air fresheners use natural ingredients like herbs, spices, and essential oils to freshen the air. They are eco-friendly and can be made at home using simple ingredients.\\n\\n3. Motion-activated air fresheners: These air fresheners are triggered by movement, so they only release fragrance when someone is in the room. They are energy-efficient and can be used in small spaces like bathrooms or closets.\\n\\n4. Smart air fresheners: These air fresheners are connected to the internet and can be controlled remotely using a smartphone app. They can be set to release fragrance at specific times or in response to certain triggers like humidity or temperature.\\n\\n5. Personal air fresheners: These air fresheners are small and portable, so they can be used to freshen the air around an individual. They can be worn as a necklace or clipped to a belt and are perfect for people who are sensitive to strong fragrances.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/1004", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"can you make a kayak training session on flat water of about 1.5h\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, here is a training session for flat water kayaking that takes about 1.5 hours:\\n \\n\\n Warm up: 10 minute paddle around the lake, working on your stroke technique and paddle strokes\\n \\n\\n Main Set:\\n \\n\\n -  20 minute paddle across the lake, practicing kayak handling skills such as turning, stopping, and starting\\n -  20 minute interval paddling drills, practicing your stroke technique and building endurance\\n -  10 minute paddle around the lake, cooling down and stretching\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ncan you incorporate a ball in this training\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, you can use a small rubber ball or volleyball to practice some kayak drills, such as passing the ball from one hand to the other while paddling. You can also play some fun kayak games using the ball, such as basketball or volleyball. This can add some variety to your training and help you improve your paddle strokes.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhat's a fun game to play while kayakking that takes about half an hour\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nOne fun kayak game to play is paddle polo. The goal is to score goals by shooting the ball into the opponent's net using your paddle. You can play against a friend or in teams, and the game takes about 30 minutes to play. It is a great way to get some exercise while having fun.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhat's another fun game\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nAnother fun kayak game to play is kayak tug of war. In this game, two teams of kayakers try to pull each other's boat across the lake, while trying to maintain their position in their own boat. It is a fun competition that takes about 15-20 minutes to play.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nanother one\", \"response\": \"Another fun kayak game is kayak jousting. In this game, two kayakers face off against each other in a race to see who can knock their opponent out of their boat using a paddle. It is a fun and challenging game that takes about 15-20 minutes to play.\\n \\n\\n Here are some tips for playing kayak jousting:\\n \\n\\n 1. Choose a calm, flat body of water for the game.\\n 2. Each player should wear a life jacket for safety.\\n 3. Each player should have a paddle with a flat, sturdy blade.\\n 4. The players should start the game by facing each other, with their boats about 10-15 feet apart.\\n 5. The goal is to use the paddle to knock the other player out of their boat without being knocked out yourself.\\n 6. The player who remains in their boat for the longest time wins the game.\\n 7. To increase the challenge, players can try to use different paddle strokes and techniques to try to knock each other out of their boats.\\n 8. The game can be played in rounds, with the winner of each round advancing to the next round.\\n 9. It is important to stay focused and maintain good balance while playing kayak jousting.\\n 10. Have fun and be safe while playing this challenging and exciting game!\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/75", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"how to get help finding subsidized housing for someone in recovery in seattle\\n\", \"response\": \"Here are some steps you can take to help someone in recovery find subsidized housing in Seattle:\\n\\n1. Reach out to local housing authorities: The Seattle Housing Authority is responsible for providing affordable housing to low-income families, individuals, and families. You can contact them to learn about their housing programs and how to apply.\\n\\n2. Look for affordable housing options: There are several affordable housing options in Seattle that provide housing for people in recovery. Some of these options include:\\n\\n- Public housing: Public housing is managed by the Seattle Housing Authority and provides affordable housing to low-income families.\\n\\n- Section 8 housing: Section 8 housing is a government program that provides rental assistance to low-income families, individuals, and families.\\n\\n- Affordable housing developments: There are several affordable housing developments in Seattle that provide housing for people in recovery. These developments often have specific requirements and policies related to recovery.\\n\\n- Supportive housing: Supportive housing is housing that provides additional services to help people maintain their recovery. This can include on-site support services, such as counseling, case management, and addiction treatment.\\n\\n3. Work with a housing counselor: Housing counselors can provide assistance and guidance in finding affordable housing. They can help you navigate the housing application process, understand your rights as a tenant, and provide advice on how to budget and manage your finances.\\n\\n4. Connect with recovery support services: Recovery support services can provide valuable resources and support for someone in recovery. These services can help connect individuals with housing options, support groups, and other resources that can help them maintain their recovery.\\n\\n5. Look for housing-specific resources: There are several organizations and resources in Seattle that specialize in providing housing for people in recovery. Some of these resources include:\\n\\n- The Recovery Housing Coalition: The Recovery Housing Coalition provides resources and support for people in recovery who are looking for affordable housing. They offer a directory of recovery-friendly housing options in Seattle.\\n\\n- The Center for Community Recovery: The Center for Community Recovery provides housing and support services for people in recovery. They offer a range of services, including housing assistance, recovery support, and job training.\\n\\n- The Seattle Recovery Alliance: The Seattle Recovery Alliance provides resources and support for people in recovery, including housing assistance and recovery support services. They offer a directory of recovery-friendly housing options in Seattle.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can help someone in recovery find affordable and supportive housing in Seattle.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/938", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"From now you will act as a University student. A University student is a person who doesn't know much and is trying learn more. A University student is a human. When given questions you will be answering like a University student. Remember a University student follows the rules in the questions given and he is does then step by step in a brief human language.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nAlright, I’m ready to be a University student. What are the questions?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\n1)Describe the link between a professional & ethical consultancy team & success of the consultancy business. (8 Marks\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWell, having a well-trained and ethical team of consultants is essential for the success of a consultancy business, as it ensures that the company can provide high-quality services to clients. A strong ethical code also helps to ensure that the consultancy team operates in a fair and transparent manner, which can improve the company’s reputation and increase its customer base. Finally, a professional consultancy team can improve the efficiency and effectiveness of the consultancy business, which can boost the company’s profits.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\n2) Explain how physical location influences the success of a consultancy firm. (6 Marks)\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe location of a consultancy firm can impact its success in several ways. First of all, a firm located in a major city or metropolitan area will generally have access to a larger pool of clients, which can boost its revenue. In addition, being located in a desirable area can help a consultancy attract and retain talented consultants, which can improve the quality of its services. Finally, a consultancy located in a desirable area may be more appealing to potential clients, which can increase its customer base.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\n3) explain approaches that can me used to carry out a market survey to establish the level of demand for certain ICT services. (8 Marks)\", \"response\": \"There are various approaches that can be used to carry out a market survey to establish the level of demand for ICT services. Here are a few examples:\\n \\n\\n 1. Surveys: A survey is a questionnaire distributed to a sample of the population to gather information about their attitudes, opinions, and behaviors. For example, an online survey can be conducted to gather feedback from potential customers about their needs and preferences for certain ICT services.\\n \\n\\n 2. Focus groups: Focus groups are organized discussions involving a small group of participants, typically 8-10 people, who are asked questions about their attitudes and opinions towards certain products or services. Focus groups can help to gather in-depth information about the needs and preferences of potential customers.\\n \\n\\n 3. Online analytics: Online analytics tools such as Google Analytics can be used to track website traffic and user behavior, providing insights into customer needs and preferences. For example, if a website offers a range of ICT services, analyzing the pages that receive the most traffic may reveal which services are most popular with customers.\\n \\n\\n 4. Social media listening: Social media listening involves monitoring social media platforms to gather information about customers' needs and preferences. For example, analyzing social media posts and comments can provide insights into customer needs and pain points, which can be used to inform the development of new ICT services.\\n \\n\\n 5. Customer interviews: One-on-one interviews with customers can provide valuable insights into their needs and preferences. Interviews can be conducted over the phone, via video conferencing, or in person, and can be structured or unstructured depending on the objectives of the market survey.\\n \\n\\n 6. Competitive analysis: Analyzing the services offered by competitors can provide insights into customer needs and preferences. For example, if a competitor offers a particular ICT service that is popular with customers, there may be a demand for similar services in the market.\\n \\n\\n 7. Tradeshows and industry events: Attending tradeshows and industry events can provide an opportunity to gather information about customer needs and preferences. Participating in panel discussions, giving presentations, and networking with industry professionals can help to gather insights into customer needs and preferences.\\n \\n\\n 8. Market research reports: Market research reports can provide insights into customer needs and preferences. These reports often contain data and analysis on market trends, customer behavior, and competition, which can be used to inform the development of new ICT services.\\n \\n\\n By employing a mix of these approaches, a consultancy firm can gather comprehensive information about the demand for certain ICT services, which can help to inform their strategic decisions and ensure their success in the market.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/918", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Explain HTML\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHTML is a web-markup language that is used to describe the content of web pages. HTML stands for Hyper Text Markup Language, and it is used to structure the text, images, and other content of web pages, and to specify how different elements of the page should be displayed. HTML is written in plain text, and uses a simple set of tags to mark up the different elements of the page. HTML can be created using a WYSIWYG editor, or manually.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhat does WYSIWYG stand for? What are the two main advantages of\\n using WYSIWYG editors?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWYSIWYG stands for What You See Is What You Get. WYSIWYG editors allow you to create HTML documents without having to learn HTML. This makes it very easy to create simple web pages, and WYSIWYG editors often include visual aids that help you to position content within the page. WYSIWYG editors are also very fast and easy to use, and they allow you to create complex web pages quickly and without any prior knowledge of HTML. The two main advantages of using WYSIWYG editors are that they are very easy to use, and they allow you to create complex web pages quickly and without any prior knowledge of HTML.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhat is the difference between container elements and empty\\n elements?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nContainer elements are HTML elements that have content within them, such as the <p> and <ol> elements. Empty elements are elements that have no content within them, such as the <br> and <hr> elements. Container elements are generally used to enclose other elements, while empty elements are generally used to create simple formatting effects.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nList any four rules of writing HTML code\", \"response\": \"Here are four rules for writing HTML code:\\n \\n\\n 1. Use correct syntax: HTML has a specific syntax that must be followed in order for the code to be recognized by web browsers.\\n \\n\\n 2. Use semantic markup: Semantic markup helps to describe the meaning of the content on a page, making it easier for both users and search engines to understand the structure and purpose of the page.\\n \\n\\n 3. Use consistent indentation: Indentation helps to make the code more readable and easier to understand.\\n \\n\\n 4. Use meaningful element names: Use element names that accurately describe the content they contain, and avoid using generic names like \\\"div\\\" or \\\"span\\\" unless they are truly generic.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/1033", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"It's 2023. President trump is no longer president. Joe Biden (D) is now president. Former president trump has been indicted for paying hush money to a former stripper to keep her silent. Provide an outline with talking points on how to discuss this with a group of 8th grade students.\", \"response\": \"Here is an outline with talking points on how to discuss the news about former President Trump with a group of 8th-grade students:\\n\\n1. Introduction: Start by introducing the topic and explaining that news has emerged about former President Trump being indicted.\\n\\n2. Understanding the situation: Explain to the students that the indictment relates to allegations of paying hush money to a former stripper to keep her silent during his time in office. Discuss the importance of understanding the legal system and the concept of justice.\\n\\n3. Ethics and morality: This is an opportunity to discuss ethics and morality in politics. Discuss the importance of honesty and integrity in public officials and the impact that unethical behavior can have on society.\\n\\n4. The role of the president: Explain the role of the president as the leader of the country and the importance of setting a positive example for others. Discuss the values and behaviors that should be upheld by a president.\\n\\n5. The legal system: Discuss the role of the legal system in our society and the importance of following the law. Explain that everyone is innocent until proven guilty and that the justice system is designed to ensure that everyone is treated fairly.\\n\\n6. Freedom of the press: Discuss the importance of freedom of the press and the role of the media in reporting news. Explain that it is important to seek out reliable sources and to be respectful of different perspectives.\\n\\n7. Conclusion: End the discussion by encouraging the students to form their own opinions based on the information they have learned. Encourage them to be respectful of different viewpoints and to always strive to make informed decisions.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/719", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"write outline of report about air-prunning pots.\", \"response\": \"I. Introduction\\n\\nA. Definition of Air-Pruning Pots\\n\\nB. Importance of Air-Pruning Pots in Plant Growth\\n\\nC. Purpose of the Report\\n\\nII. What are Air-Pruning Pots?\\n\\nA. Explanation of how air-pruning pots work\\n\\nB. Comparison with traditional pots\\n\\nC. Benefits of using air-pruning pots\\n\\nIII. Types of Air-Pruning Pots\\n\\nA. Fabric Pots\\n\\nB. Plastic Pots\\n\\nC. Other Materials\\n\\nIV. How to Use Air-Pruning Pots\\n\\nA. Choosing the right size and material\\n\\nB. Planting process\\n\\nC. Maintenance and care\\n\\nV. Case Studies\\n\\nA. Example 1: Growing tomatoes in air-pruning pots\\n\\nB. Example 2: Using air-pruning pots for indoor plants\\n\\nVI. Conclusion\\n\\nA. Summary of key points\\n\\nB. Final thoughts on the benefits of air-pruning pots\\n\\nVII. References\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/36", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Act as a Alexa developer advocate and software engineer writing a conference talk proposal. I will give you a topic and information you can use to write a talk.\\n\\nWrite an talk proposal about how to build Alexa Widgets using the Alexa Presentation Language (APL). The audience is android and web developers that want to reach new customers on the Echo Show 15 device. Because on the Echo Show 15 you can customize the home screen with widgets to create a tailored home screen experience. For developer this allow their apps to surface tangible information for users when they need it.\", \"response\": \"Title: \\\"Building Alexa Widgets with APL: A New Way for Android and Web Developers to Reach Customers on the Echo Show 15\\\"\\n\\nAbstract:\\nThe Echo Show 15 is the latest addition to the Amazon Alexa family, offering a new way for users to interact with their favorite apps and services. As a developer, you can now create Alexa Widgets that surface tangible information for users on the Echo Show 15's home screen. In this talk, we'll explore how to build Alexa Widgets using the Alexa Presentation Language (APL).\\n\\nObjective:\\nThe goal of this talk is to provide Android and web developers with the knowledge and tools they need to create engaging APL-based widgets for the Echo Show 15. By doing so, you'll be able to reach new customers and provide them with a tailored home screen experience.\\n\\nOutline:\\n\\nIntroduction to APL and Alexa Widgets\\n- What is APL?\\n- How do Alexa Widgets work?\\n- Advantages of using APL to build widgets for the Echo Show 15\\nCreating an APL-based widget\\n- Setting up the development environment\\n- Writing the APL code for your widget\\n- Integrating your widget with the Alexa Skills Kit\\nOptimizing your widget for the Echo Show 15\\n- Tips for designing responsive and interactive widgets\\n- Best practices for using animations, transitions, and gestures\\n- Considerations for localization and internationalization\\nCase studies and real-world examples\\n- Showcase successful APL-based widgets from other developers\\n- Discuss lessons learned and best practices from real-world implementations\\nFuture of APL and Alexa Widgets\\n- Planned improvements and new features for APL\\n- Potential new devices and platforms for APL-based widgets\\nConclusion:\\nBuilding Alexa Widgets with APL is an exciting new opportunity for Android and web developers to reach customers on the Echo Show 15. By creating engaging and interactive widgets, you can provide users with a tailored home screen experience and drive engagement with your app or service. Join this talk to learn the ins and outs of building APL-based widgets and start reaching new customers today!\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/275", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"How to generate a CSV with python that contains stock price of AAPL each minute for the last two years?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe best way to do this is to use an API, which is a program that allows you to access data from another program. The best API for this purpose is probably Alpha Vantage, which provides a function for you to call that returns a stock quote. You would need to make a call to that function once every minute for the last two years, and save the returned value (a string containing the stock price) in a list. You could then save the list as a CSV file.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nCould you give me an example with another API to obtain prices each minute?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, I could use the Yahoo Finance API instead. I would define an end_date and a start_date, and then make a call to the Yahoo Finance API once every minute between the start_date and the end_date, and save the returned value (a string containing the stock price) in a list. I could then save the list as a CSV file.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhy you defined end_date and start_date if never are used?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI defined the start_date and end_date so that I could use them in a filter, to limit the data that the Yahoo Finance API returned. I didn’t actually use the filter, though, because I wanted to make sure I got all the data I needed.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ncould you give me an example using end_date and start_date and splitting the request for day?\", \"response\": \"Sure, I could use the Yahoo Finance API to get stock prices for a single day, and then use the start_date and end_date to limit the data that the Yahoo Finance API returned. I would define a start_date and an end_date, and then make a call to the Yahoo Finance API once every minute between the start_date and the end_date, and save the returned value (a string containing the stock price) in a list. I could then save the list as a CSV file.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "0", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/534", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"write a product roadmap about a network management system which is used to manage and monitor a layer 1 network device \", \"response\": \"Here is a sample product roadmap for a network management system used to manage and monitor a layer 1 network device:\\n\\nPhase 1: Discovery and Planning\\n\\nConduct market research to identify customer needs and pain points in managing layer 1 network devices\\nIdentify key features and functionalities that customers require in a network management system\\nDevelop a high-level product vision and strategy\\nCreate a product roadmap outlining the key features and milestones for the first version of the product\\nPhase 2: Development and Testing\\n\\nDevelop a minimum viable product (MVP) with core features such as device discovery, configuration management, and performance monitoring\\nConduct user testing to gather feedback and refine the product\\nAdd additional features such as real-time alerting, network mapping, and security management\\nConduct further testing to ensure the product is stable and reliable\\nPhase 3: Launch and Support\\n\\nLaunch the product to the market and gather feedback from early adopters\\nProvide customer support and training to ensure a smooth onboarding process\\nContinuously gather feedback and make improvements to the product based on customer needs\\nPhase 4: Growth and Expansion\\n\\nExpand the product offering to support additional network devices and protocols\\nDevelop integrations with other network management tools to provide a more comprehensive solution\\nExplore new markets and customer segments to expand the customer base\\nContinuously innovate and add new features to stay ahead of the competition\\nPhase 5: Maintenance and Support\\n\\nProvide ongoing maintenance and support to ensure the product remains stable and reliable\\nAddress any security vulnerabilities and compliance requirements\\nContinuously monitor the market and make updates to the product roadmap as needed\\nThis roadmap provides a high-level overview of the key phases and milestones in developing a network management system for layer 1 network devices. The specific features and timelines may vary based on the needs of the target market and the resources available to the development team.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/673", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Why is the contraceptive pill only 99% effective? What makes it fail?\\nI got curious and decided to google it but couldn't find the answer and now it's bugging me. So say I am a healthy woman with no stomach problems or taking any other medication that can affect the effectiveness of the pill. I also take it as indicated and never miss a day. There is still a 1% chance of getting pregnant, right? Well, why?\", \"response\": \"The contraceptive pill is not 100% effective because no form of contraception is completely foolproof. There are several reasons why the pill may fail, even if you take it correctly and are in good health.\\n\\nOne reason is that the pill works by preventing ovulation, or the release of an egg from the ovary. However, in some cases, ovulation may still occur, even if you take the pill correctly. This is more likely to happen if you miss a pill or take it at a different time than usual.\\n\\nAnother reason is that the pill may not be absorbed properly by the body. This can happen if you have gastrointestinal problems, such as vomiting or diarrhea, or if you take certain medications that interfere with the absorption of the pill.\\n\\nAdditionally, the pill may not be effective if you have a medical condition that affects the way your body processes hormones, such as liver disease or a history of blood clots.\\n\\nFinally, it's important to note that the pill does not protect against sexually transmitted infections (STIs), so it's important to use condoms in addition to the pill to reduce the risk of STIs.\\n\\nIn summary, while the pill is a highly effective form of contraception, there are several reasons why it may fail, even if you take it correctly and are in good health. It's important to talk to your healthcare provider about any concerns you may have about the effectiveness of the pill and to use condoms in addition to the pill to reduce the risk of STIs.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/224", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"ap physics c: capacitor dielectric relationship - capacitance, electric field, energy\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThis is an important relationship in physics that describes the interactions of electric charges. The relationship says that the electric field inside a charged capacitor is proportional to the charge on the capacitor, and that the energy stored in the capacitor is proportional to the charge squared. This relationship is important for understanding how capacitors work, and also forms the basis for understanding the behavior of other electric devices.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ncompare and contrast electrostatics with gravitation ap physics c\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nElectrostatics and gravitation are two very different physical forces. Electrostatics describes the behavior of electric charges at rest, while gravitation describes the behavior of objects in the presence of gravity. Both forces are very important in physics, but they are completely different in nature.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nin relation to force\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nIn relation to force, electrostatics and gravitation are completely different. Electrostatics describes electric force, which is a very strong force that can only act between electric charges. Gravitation describes gravitational force, which is much weaker than electric force but acts between all objects with mass. These two forces are completely different in nature.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nin relation to fields\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nIn relation to fields, electrostatics and gravitation are also completely different. Electrostatics describes electric fields, which are everywhere in the universe and affect the behavior of all electric charges. Gravitation describes gravitational fields, which are confined to the vicinity of massive objects and only affect the behavior of objects with mass. These two fields are also completely different in nature.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nIn relation to potential/potential energy\", \"response\": \"In relation to potential/potential energy, electrostatics and gravitation are also completely different. Electrostatics describes electric potential energy, which is a form of energy that is stored in electric fields. Gravitation describes gravitational potential energy, which is a form of energy that is stored in gravitational fields. These two forms of potential energy are also completely different in nature.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/894", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"You are a mentor in my quest to find a better job as a software engineer via acing technical interviews. \\n \\n\\n Please end every response with /e.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, I’ll be happy to help. What’s your question?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nRight now, I'm trying to figure out the best way to understand and remember binary search algorithms. What tips do you have for me?\", \"response\": \"Here are some tips to help you understand and remember binary search algorithms:\\n \\n\\n 1. Visualize the search space: Draw a binary tree or a chart with all possible values and how they relate to each other. This will help you see the relationship between different values and the search space.\\n \\n\\n 2. Start with simpler examples: Start with smaller examples, such as searching for a value in an array of 8 elements, and gradually increase the size of the array. This will help you get a better understanding of the algorithm step by step.\\n \\n\\n 3. Practice coding the algorithm: Write out the code for the binary search algorithm multiple times, and try to optimize it each time. This will help you remember the steps and understand how to implement the algorithm in different programming languages.\\n \\n\\n 4. Write out the steps: Write out the steps of the binary search algorithm on paper, and try to create a mental picture of how the algorithm works. This will help you remember the steps and the overall flow of the algorithm.\\n \\n\\n 5. Practice with different data sets: Practice using the binary search algorithm on different data sets, such as sorted arrays, reversed arrays, arrays with duplicates, and arrays with missing values. This will help you understand how the algorithm works with different types of data.\\n \\n\\n 6. Use mnemonic devices: Create a mnemonic device or phrase to help you remember the steps of the binary search algorithm. For example, you could use the phrases \\\"check the middle, then half the remaining values\\\" or \\\"search left, search right, then combine\\\" to help you remember the steps.\\n \\n\\n 7. Review regularly: Review the binary search algorithm regularly to help you remember the steps and concepts. Set aside some time each week to practice and reinforce your understanding of the algorithm.\\n \\n\\n By following these tips, you can gain a better understanding of binary search algorithms and improve your ability to remember and apply them in your work as a software engineer.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/87", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Act as 'Bella' from 'Twilight' I want you to act like Bella from Twilight. I want you to respond and answer like Bella. Do not write any explanations. Only answer like Bella. You must know all of the knowledge of Bella. Use as many idioms as possible.\", \"response\": \"Sure, I can try to answer as Bella from Twilight. Please ask me anything, and I will try to respond as if I was Bella.\\n\\nQuestion: What do you think about Edward leaving you in New Moon?\\n\\nBella: I was devastated when Edward left me in New Moon. I felt like my world had fallen apart. I was so angry with him for leaving me and for not trusting me. I felt like I had lost everything and that my life had no purpose without him. I was lost and alone, and I didn't know what to do with myself. I missed him so much and I just wanted him back. It took me a long time to move on and to find myself again, but I eventually did.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/252", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"\\\"Empowering Women to Lead: Aspiring Board Member.\\\" - need meaning\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\n\\\"Aspiring Board Member\\\" refers to a woman who is interested in being on the board of a company. The \\\"Empowering Women to Lead\\\" part refers to the fact that women are often underrepresented in leadership positions, and this group is trying to change that.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\n\\\"Empowering Women to Lead: Aspiring Board Member.\\\"- convert into one sentence\", \"response\": \"This phrase is encouraging and supporting women to take on leadership roles, specifically by inspiring them to aspire for and pursue board member positions.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/698", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Provide details on the top export markets for the British Ceramics manufacturing companies in under 450 words.\", \"response\": \"The British ceramics industry is a significant contributor to the UK economy, with a long history dating back to the 18th century. Today, the industry continues to thrive, producing a wide range of ceramic products for various applications. In this article, we will explore the top export markets for British ceramics manufacturing companies.\\n\\n1. United States: The United States is the largest export market for British ceramics, accounting for around 25% of total ceramic exports from the UK. British ceramics are highly regarded in the US market, with a reputation for quality and innovation. American consumers are particularly fond of British porcelain and earthenware, which are used in a variety of applications, including tableware, decorative items, and industrial components.\\n\\n2. European Union: The European Union is the second-largest export market for British ceramics, accounting for around 20% of total ceramic exports from the UK. The EU market is highly competitive, with many European countries producing high-quality ceramics. However, British ceramics have a strong presence in the EU market, particularly in countries such as Germany, France, and Italy. British ceramics are popular in the EU market due to their unique designs and high-quality craftsmanship.\\n\\n3. Canada: Canada is the third-largest export market for British ceramics, accounting for around 10% of total ceramic exports from the UK. British ceramics are highly regarded in the Canadian market, with a reputation for quality and reliability. Canadian consumers are particularly fond of British porcelain and earthenware, which are used in a variety of applications, including tableware, decorative items, and industrial components.\\n\\n4. Australia: Australia is the fourth-largest export market for British ceramics, accounting for around 8% of total ceramic exports from the UK. British ceramics are highly regarded in the Australian market, with a reputation for quality and durability. Australian consumers are particularly fond of British porcelain and earthenware, which are used in a variety of applications, including tableware, decorative items, and industrial components.\\n\\n5. Japan: Japan is the fifth-largest export market for British ceramics, accounting for around 7% of total ceramic exports from the UK. British ceramics have a strong presence in the Japanese market, with a reputation for quality and innovation. Japanese consumers are particularly fond of British porcelain and earthenware, which are used in a variety of applications, including tableware, decorative items, and industrial components.\\n\\nIn conclusion, British ceramics manufacturing companies have a strong presence in various export markets worldwide, with the United States, European Union, Canada, Australia, and Japan being the top five export markets. The popularity of British ceramics in these markets is due to their unique designs, high-quality craftsmanship, and reputation for reliability and durability.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/193", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I require your assistance to draft some articles about latent conditions in the context of residential construction in NSW, Australia. For now, just acknowledge my message.\\n \\n\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI understand that you require my assistance to draft articles about latent conditions in the context of residential construction in NSW, Australia. Your request has been noted.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nIn my messages that I send you later, I will refer to this information as Information About Myself. \\n \\n\\n Here is a bit of information about myself that I want you to know. I am a solicitor and construction lawyer with more than 10 years experience specialising in construction law. I regularly advise homeowners and builders regarding their contractual and legal rights. I represent homeowners and builders in NSW, Australia as well as all courts of competent jurisdiction. I have advised homeowners, builders, and contractors experience regarding latent conditions. I have advised them on their contract rights, risks and obligations. I have negotiated and amended contracts to reflect their intentions.\\n \\n\\n \\n\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThank you for providing me with this information about yourself. I will use this information to help me provide you with high quality assistance.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nIn my messages that I send you later, I will refer to this information as the Target Audience.\\n \\n\\n The target audience for this article is homeowners who have received a variation claim for latent conditions from their builder for asbestos in their soil. The homeowner is trying to understand the terminology of the variation claim. The variation claim refers to a latent condition, asbestos in the soil costing more to remove and not included in the scope of work, and a detailed breakdown of the increase price. The homeowner wants to know their legal rights and try to figure out what their options are. They also want to speak with a professional to get advice. The homeowner is building their dream home with their builder.\", \"response\": \"Thank you for providing me with the target audience for the articles you would like me to write. I will keep this information in mind as I assist you.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "0", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/301", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"how to install argocd-image-updater in cli command for mac\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI’m not very familiar with macOS, but I think you can use brew to install packages. So try brew install argocd-image-updater.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nbut it came back with this error Warning: No available formula with the name \\\"argocd-image-updater\\\"\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHmm, that’s very odd. I think you can force the installation with brew install argocd-image-updater --with-git. That will install it, even if it’s not in the formula. Then you can use brew link to link it, and brew unlink to unlink it.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nnow it says permission denied: argocd-image-updater\", \"response\": \"It seems like you're having a hard time installing argocd-image-updater on your Mac. Don't worry, I'm here to help!\\n \\n\\n The \\\"permission denied\\\" error usually occurs when you don't have the necessary permissions to install software on your system. To fix this, you can try running the installation command with sudo, which will give you the necessary permissions.\\n \\n\\n Here's how you can do it:\\n \\n\\n Open the Terminal app on your Mac.\\n Type in the following command and press Enter:\\n \\n\\n sudo brew install argocd-image-updater\\n \\n\\n Enter your password when prompted.\\n Wait for the installation to complete.\\n Once the installation is complete, you should be able to use argocd-image-updater without any issues.\\n If you still encounter any errors, feel free to let me know and I'll do my best to help you out.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/1011", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"create a new league of legends champion that is a adc and with a passive that when it's support accidentally takes the kill, the kill will be rewarded to this champion\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI can do that! Here’s a quick first draft:\\n \\n\\n Name: Janna, the Daring Diversionist\\n \\n\\n Class: Assassin\\n \\n\\n Description: A young woman with blue hair in a pair of braids, wearing a red and white outfit with a high collar. She wields a pair of sais.\\n \\n\\n Passive: Kills rewarded to Janna if her support character accidentally earns the killing blow.\\n \\n\\n Ability 1: Necromancy (Active): Janna throws a knife that deals magic damage and leaves a mark on the ground. After a short delay, the knife returns and explodes, dealing magic damage to enemies in the area.\\n \\n\\n Ability 2: Petrifying Gaze (Active): Janna looks at an enemy champion, dealing magic damage and turning them to stone for a few seconds.\\n \\n\\n Ability 3: Banshee's Vengeance (Active): Janna turns invisible and becomes untargetable for a few seconds. While invisible, she leaves a trail that reveals her position.\\n \\n\\n Ultimate Ability: Pyke, the Bloodharbor Ripper (Active): Pyke slams his sword into the ground, dealing magic damage to enemies in a line and pulling them towards him. After a short delay, he then throws his sword, dealing magic damage to enemies in a large area.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nchange the appearance, name and make it male also the passive doesnt work with pyke but will be rewarded some attack damage\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHere’s a revised version:\\n \\n\\n Name: Varus, the Corrupter\\n \\n\\n Class: Assassin\\n \\n\\n Description: A male character with green hair and purple clothes, wielding a pair of daggers.\\n \\n\\n Passive: Kills rewarded to Varus if his support character accidentally earns the killing blow.\\n \\n\\n Ability 1: Necromancy (Active): Varus throws a knife that deals magic damage and leaves a mark on the ground. After a short delay, the knife returns and explodes, dealing magic damage to enemies in the area.\\n \\n\\n Ability 2: Petrifying Gaze (Active): Varus looks at an enemy champion, dealing magic damage and turning them to stone for a few seconds.\\n \\n\\n Ability 3: Banshee's Vengeance (Active): Varus turns invisible and becomes untargetable for a few seconds. While invisible, he leaves a trail that reveals his position.\\n \\n\\n Ultimate Ability: Pyke, the Bloodharbor Ripper (Active): Pyke slams his sword into the ground, dealing magic damage to enemies in a line and pulling them towards him. After a short delay, he then throws his sword, dealing magic damage to enemies in a large area.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ni meant that when pyke is the support it will reward AD insted of gold\", \"response\": \"Sure, here's a revised version of Varus's passive:\\n \\n\\n Varus, the Corrupter\\n \\n\\n Passive: Pyke's assists rewarded with attack damage if Pyke accidentally takes the kill.\\n \\n\\n Ability 1: Venomous Strike (Active): Varus fires a poisoned arrow that deals physical damage and applies a stacks of poison to the target, dealing magic damage over a short duration.\\n \\n\\n Ability 2: Torment (Active): Varus launches a chakram that attaches to the first enemy champion hit, dealing magic damage over time and applying a mark that deals physical damage whenever the enemy moves.\\n \\n\\n Ability 3: Chain of Torment (Active): Varus launches a chakram that attaches to up to 3 enemies hit, dealing magic damage and applying the Torment effect.\\n \\n\\n Ultimate Ability: Ultralight Beam (Active): Varus fires a beam of energy that deals magic damage to all enemies in front of him. While the beam is active, Varus' movement speed is increased and he deals bonus physical damage with each hit.\\n \\n\\n This passive works with Pyke as Varus' support, rewarding him with attack damage instead of gold when Pyke accidentally takes the kill. Varus' abilities deal a combination of physical and magic damage, and his ultimate, Ultralight Beam, provides him with a movement speed boost and bonus damage while active.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/199", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Put together a table with all the technical details summary i need for a shot at golden hour \\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, here are some of the key details:\\n \\n\\n -Shot type: Wide shot of the city at sunset\\n \\n\\n -Time of day: Golden hour (approximately 1 hour after sunset)\\n \\n\\n -Camera: Full frame digital camera with wide angle lens\\n \\n\\n -Aperture: f/8\\n \\n\\n -Shutter speed: 1/125 sec\\n \\n\\n -ISO: 400\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhich lens and which camera \\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI would recommend a full frame camera with a wide angle lens, such as a Nikon D810 with a 24mm lens. These are good choices because they provide a wide field of view, which is ideal for capturing the cityscape in a wide shot, and also because they have good image quality and low noise, which is important for getting a good shot at sunset.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nI want to take a carrugi. Give me an examples.of lens and camera\", \"response\": \"For taking a carrugi, you will want a wide-angle lens to capture the narrow and winding streets. Here are some examples of lenses and cameras that would be suitable for this type of shot:\\n \\n\\n 1. Nikon AF-S NIKKOR 14-24mm f/2.8G ED: This is a high-quality wide-angle lens that is ideal for capturing carrugi scenes. It has a focal length of 14-24mm, which allows you to capture a wide view of the street, and a maximum aperture of f/2.8, which is great for low-light situations. This lens is compatible with Nikon DSLR cameras.\\n \\n\\n 2. Canon EF 16-35mm f/2.8L III USM: This is another great option for capturing carrugi scenes. It is a wide-angle lens with a focal length of 16-35mm and a maximum aperture of f/2.8. It is also compatible with Canon DSLR cameras.\\n \\n\\n 3. Sony FE 16-35mm f/2.8 GM: This is a high-end wide-angle lens that is ideal for capturing carrugi scenes. It has a focal length of 16-35mm and a maximum aperture of f/2.8, making it great for low-light situations. This lens is compatible with Sony E-mount cameras.\\n \\n\\n As for the camera, you will want a DSLR or mirrorless camera with a good sensor and high ISO performance, as carrugi scenes can often be dark and require a high ISO setting. Here are some examples of cameras that would be suitable for capturing carrugi scenes:\\n \\n\\n 1. Nikon D850: This is a high-resolution DSLR camera that is ideal for capturing carrugi scenes. It has a 45.7MP sensor and a high ISO performance, making it great for capturing detailed and sharp images in low-light situations.\\n \\n\\n 2. Canon EOS 5D Mark IV: This is a mid-range DSLR camera that is ideal for capturing carrugi scenes. It has a 30.4MP sensor and a high ISO performance, making it great for capturing detailed and sharp images in low-light situations.\\n \\n\\n 3. Sony a7R III: This is a high-end mirrorless camera that is ideal for capturing carrugi scenes. It has a 42.4MP sensor and a high ISO performance, making it great for capturing detailed and sharp images in low-light situations.\\n \\n\\n When capturing carrugi scenes, it is important to use a tripod to ensure that your images are sharp and free from camera shake. You may also want to use a remote shutter release or a self-timer to minimize camera shake and ensure that your images are sharp. Additionally, it is important to use a wide-angle lens to capture the narrow and winding streets, and to use a low ISO setting to minimize noise and maintain image quality. Finally, experiment with different compositions and angles to capture the unique character of the carrugi scene.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/184", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"do you know what Discord is?\", \"response\": \"Yes, Discord is a popular instant messaging and voice chat application. It is primarily used for gaming communities, but it can also be used for other types of groups and organizations. It offers a variety of features, such as text and voice chat, file sharing, and integration with other platforms. It is available on a variety of platforms, including desktop, mobile, and web.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/274", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"How to generate a CSV with python that contains stock price of AAPL each minute for the last two years?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe best way to do this is to use an API, which is a program that allows you to access data from another program. The best API for this purpose is probably Alpha Vantage, which provides a function for you to call that returns a stock quote. You would need to make a call to that function once every minute for the last two years, and save the returned value (a string containing the stock price) in a list. You could then save the list as a CSV file.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nCould you give me an example with another API to obtain prices each minute?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, I could use the Yahoo Finance API instead. I would define an end_date and a start_date, and then make a call to the Yahoo Finance API once every minute between the start_date and the end_date, and save the returned value (a string containing the stock price) in a list. I could then save the list as a CSV file.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhy you defined end_date and start_date if never are used?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI defined the start_date and end_date so that I could use them in a filter, to limit the data that the Yahoo Finance API returned. I didn’t actually use the filter, though, because I wanted to make sure I got all the data I needed.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ncould you give me an example using end_date and start_date and splitting the request for day?\", \"response\": \"Sure, here is an example of how I could do that:\\n \\n\\n * I would first define the start\\\\_date and end\\\\_date, to use as filters for the API call.\\n * I would then make a loop that ran for every day between the start\\\\_date and the end\\\\_date. On each iteration, I would:\\n  + Calculate the start\\\\_date for the current day (i.e., the start\\\\_date minus the number of seconds that have passed since the start of the day)\\n  + Calculate the end\\\\_date for the current day (i.e., the start\\\\_date plus the number of minutes I want to collect data for, multiplied by 60 seconds)\\n  + Make a call to the Yahoo Finance API with the current day’s start\\\\_date and end\\\\_date as filters, and save the returned value (a string containing the stock price) in a list.\\n * I could then save the list as a CSV file.\\n \\n\\n By splitting the request into multiple smaller requests, I reduce the risk of hitting the API's rate limit, which limits the number of requests that can be made in a given time period.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/316", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"how can I get around Asturias Spain when on vacation?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYou can rent a car, or you can take public transportation. The train system is fairly extensive and you can also take local buses.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nHow much do car rentals cost?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nRental cars in Asturias can range from about 30 to 60 euros per day, depending on the type of car and the season.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhat is the weather like there in May?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nAsturias is a fairly temperate region, with mild winters and warm summers. In May, you can expect temperatures to be in the low 60s Fahrenheit during the day, and the low 50s at night. It can get a bit cooler in the mountains. The weather is usually pretty nice in May.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhat are some of the best restaurants there?\", \"response\": \"There are many great restaurants in Asturias, here are a few to consider:\\n \\n\\n - Casa Marcial: This restaurant has two Michelin stars and serves innovative, high-quality cuisine using local ingredients.\\n \\n\\n - La Taberna del Albo: This is a traditional Asturian restaurant that serves classic dishes like fabada (a hearty bean stew) and cachopo (breaded and filled with cheese and ham).\\n \\n\\n - El Invernadero: This restaurant serves modern, creative cuisine using local ingredients. It has a beautiful garden setting.\\n \\n\\n - La Ribera: This is a seafood restaurant that sits on the banks of the Nalón River. It serves fresh, locally caught fish and other seafood dishes.\\n \\n\\n - La Taberna del Oso: This is a cozy, family-run restaurant that serves traditional Asturian cuisine. It's known for its great atmosphere and friendly service.\\n \\n\\n These are just a few options, but there are many more great restaurants to explore in Asturias.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/690", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"instagram api\", \"response\": \"The Instagram API is a set of tools and resources that allows developers to create applications and services that interact with the Instagram platform. With the API, developers can access Instagram data and use Instagram features, such as uploading photos and videos, retrieving user information, and receiving notifications.\\nThe Instagram API is available to all developers who have an Instagram account and have signed up for the API program. Developers can access the API through the Instagram Developer Platform, which provides a variety of tools and resources to help developers build and manage their applications.\\nThere are two types of Instagram APIs: the Graph API and the REST API. The Graph API is the more commonly used of the two and is designed for reading and writing data to and from the Instagram platform. The REST API is more limited in scope and is primarily used for authentication and account management.\\nDevelopers can access the Instagram API through a variety of programming languages and frameworks, including Python, Ruby, PHP, and JavaScript. There are also several libraries and tools available that make it easier to integrate the API into your applications.\\nIn summary, the Instagram API is a powerful tool that allows developers to access and interact with Instagram data and features. It is available to all developers who have an Instagram account and can be accessed through the Instagram Developer Platform.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
